{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1444399-unclear-about-how-marionette-works","id":1444399,"title":"Unclear about how marionette works","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-17T16:19:50-07:00","id":1444399,"title":"Unclear about how marionette works","content":"Hi,<br /> <br /> one of my players is a bound with the Marionette haunt, and he's using it sort of as a multitool. Attach marionette to a lock, use it as a lockpick. Since the locks whole purpose is locking and unlocking, he's just making it do what it's supposed to. Attach it to an electrical device like a computer, use it to hack. The hacking he justified with the example of possessing someone else's phone from page 109 of the core rulebook. For now i just let him do it because i didn't want to punish him for using his skills creatively, but i told him i would look into it and may change my ruling for future uses of marionette.<br /> How does Marionette work mechanically? Can you really use it as a jack of all traits skill to circumvent a lot of skill-checks or occasions where you'd normally have to use a specific tool or knowledge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26792-bernd","name":"Bernd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T17:03:56-07:00","id":1444408,"title":"","content":"As per the rules, yes. It gives you full and total control of an object including the moving parts. It's probably the most versatile power sin-eaters have. In order to compete against this without houserules, you'd have to come up with powers or abilities that block magical manipulation.<br /> <br /> Edit-However, in the case of hacking a phone. I'd still make a basic skill check if the data is hidden in the phone. Checking someone's contacts is easy, finding a specific folder might be more difficult. Similarly, if you're deactivating an alarm system, I'd make a roll to check if any other alarm systems are also up. Just because you know how to hack something, doesn't necessarily mean you understand how it works. Sometimes people employ multiple alarm systems to protect something extremely valuable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-17-2021, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T18:19:10-07:00","id":1444420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bernd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1444399-unclear-about-how-marionette-works#post1444399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does Marionette work mechanically? Can you really use it as a jack of all traits skill to circumvent a lot of skill-checks or occasions where you'd normally have to use a specific tool or knowledge?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure how you'd get around needing a specific tool on a tool-using application of Marionette, but yes, the normal operations of an object with Marionette use Synergy + Marionette. It's magic. The tool &quot;knows&quot; how to do things it normally does. The main obstacle to using it for hacking is that hacking isn't a thing most computers can normally do like smartphones searching their browser history.<br /> <br /> The nature of the jack-of-all-trades application of the Haunt is that 1) unless you're unlocking it with a Key, you're rocking a fairly standard 3-6 dice pool that can't be specialized further, 2) it costs Plasm where mundane Skills wouldn't, and 3) this is a telekinesis and remote-control power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}